# Frontends

## `velora-frontend` (end-user PWA + platform admin)

- React 19 + Vite 7 + Zustand + Tailwind **v4**.
- HTTP: axios (`src/services/api.ts`) → `/api/v1`, Bearer + refresh.
- SignalR in stores: `/chatHub`, `/callHub` via `accessTokenFactory`.
- Tokens in `localStorage`: `token`, `refreshToken`, `user`.
- No `@/` alias — relative imports.
- Dev proxy → `http://localhost:5002`.
- Env: `VITE_API_URL`, optional `VITE_ENABLE_MESSAGE_LENGTH_LIMIT`.
- Scripts: `npm run dev|build|lint|preview`.

## `admin-panel` (company widget SaaS)

- Next.js 14 App Router + Zustand + Tailwind **v3**.
- HTTP: `fetch` in `src/lib/api.ts` (not axios). Alias `@/*`.
- Company auth: `X-Company-Token` + `widget_admin_company` in localStorage.
- Support auth: Bearer + `widget_admin_support`; hubs via `?access_token=`.
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (see `.env.local.example`).
- Scripts: `npm run dev|build|start|lint`.
- Plan limits may still use `MOCK_PLANS`; APIs for company/support/AI widget are real.

## Shared rules

- Match existing `ApiResponse<T>` envelope (`success`, `data`, `message`, `operationDate`).
- After API/SignalR contract changes, update the correct app only.
- Do not “unify” the two frontends’ HTTP stacks without an explicit request.
